      "writtenOn": "2026-11-21T16:59:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You\u0027re right that the series introduces a new permission — there\u0027s no existing one to reuse. Every current ChangePermission is per-action (abandon, addPatchSet, editTopicName, etc.).\n\nNone is a coarse \"write the change\" gate. Writing a change\u0027s metadata had no ACL guarding it, unlike a git ref, so this adds the missing one.\n\nIt\u0027s the change-level counterpart to the ref-level ACLs on git refs — same idea, an ACL that must permit the write — but it\u0027s a ChangePermission, resolved through AbstractChangeControl just like canAbandon() (owner, branch/project owner and admin are exempt), and enforced at the NoteDb change-write chokepoint in BatchUpdate rather than as a ref-level check on refs/changes/*/meta.\n\nThat\u0027s deliberate: the chokepoint is the one place every logical change write funnels through, so one guard covers them all.\n\nSo nothing contradicts \"leaving the ACL evaluation model unchanged\": a new permission is added to the set, but the machinery that resolves any permission — and ALLOW/BLOCK precedence — is untouched.",
      "parentUuid": "f2230925_668cc8e1",
